### Testing Strategy

The plugin's default testing strategy is **derived from the functional core / imperative shell commitment**, not designed independently:

- **Pure-core unit tests**: values in, values out, no mocks. One per pure-core function.
- **Shell integration tests**: real I/O against real dependencies (test DB, tmpdir, fake-backed HTTP from recorded real calls). Mocks only at hard external boundaries (third-party APIs without sandboxes, cost-bearing services, hardware absent in test).
- **No internal-module mocks.** A "unit test" that needs a mock for an internal collaborator means the core/shell boundary is wrong — fix the architecture.

